A||||8||Banzai||Front control arm bolt sizes???||||5||
Z||000000||Banzai||10-29-2001||07:23 PM||||Anyone have the front lower control arm bolt sizes?? I have to make a trip to my local hardware supplier to get the metric bolts. Having the sizes would be easier. Thanks<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Nashco||10-29-2001||07:45 PM||||I just had to get some for mine.  The stock bolts are 12mm x 1.25mm x 90mm, I believe.  Does this sound right to anybody/everybody else?  Don't take my word for this too quickly, as my memory is a little foggy.  All I know is I (in a pinch) tried to use some american stuff to get by temporarily.  The 7/16" were sloppy, and the 1/2" was too big.  You can get whatever thread you want to, that doesn't matter, as long as you get all new nuts.  You should also try to get locknuts of some sort.  I forgot to, because I was so happy to have the right bolts finally...I plan on getting them soon, but in the meantime smothered the end of the bolt with RTV silicone in case anything does loosen up, and I check on it weekly.<P>So, can somebody verify this?<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tigger||10-29-2001||11:03 PM||||I got control arm bolts at Mid-State Bolt and Screw.  South East corner of I-475 and Bristol Rd, the building is set back from the road.  They have the factory 10.9 POR hardness bolts in almost any 10mm increment length.  12mm x 1.25mm I think is correct.  90-100mm long sounds about right too, I'd take a quick measure across the bracket to be sure.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Banzai||10-30-2001||11:10 AM||||Thanks guys. That's (Midstate) where I was headed Tigger, they've never let me down when I needed something. Haven't had to go there in a while, Home Depot and Lowes are closer to me.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000004||lowCG||10-30-2001||11:11 PM||||Ahh,the availability of car stuff in MI...<BR>Sniffle,at least I got my motor while I was there.<BR>I remember turning down some standard bolts on a lathe in a bad memory somewhere.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Nashco||10-31-2001||02:43 AM||||LowCG...if all you needed was hardware, nut and bolt stores are all over around there!!!  I lived in Snohomish for a long time, and I know that there are two nut and bolt stores within a couple miles of each other in downtown Everett!  I also know there's a hardware supply store right ON I-5 around Lynnwood on the southbound side called "Tacoma Screw" which happens to be a brance of Tacoma Screw that's in Tacoma.  Look in the phone book! LOL, I'm sure you'll find them <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Whoa...crazy, I just remembered, I still have my ticket from the waiting line at the hardware store in Everett!!!  That was almost two years ago...the reason I saved it is because I was buying hardware for my 1969 VW Bug, and I got number 69...and 69 is just a good number to have...so I kept it to chuckle at now and again.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-31-2001||08:26 AM||||I got an origional GM replacement for $20. canadian ($1.99 US?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> )<BR>As fas as I know the GM replacements are made of a stronger steel.<P> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Tigger||10-31-2001||08:48 AM||||I know, I checked the local Pontaic dealer and they wanted about $10 for every bolt and nut!  Then they told me I would have to wait because they had to "special" order them.<P>So instead of waiting to give the dealer $80 for 4 bolts and 4 nuts.  I got everything for about $8.00 at the supply store.<P>I can't imagine the bolts not being as strong as the factory replacements when they have the same factory harness stamped on the head?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif">||||reg||1
